# environments and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Run artifacts. Reproducible from design.yaml plus the pinned environment, and
# a single die-level run writes tens of megabytes.
**/runs/

# --- The IP boundary, enforced here and not by recollection -----------------
#
# Everything under projects/ is proprietary to its scope and MUST NOT be
# published. The exclusion below was commented out until 2026-08-11, which meant
# a first commit of this repository would have published client work. It is now
# active, and it is not to be relaxed.
#
# The files remain on disk where they are: tools/check_ip_boundary.py reads
# projects/<scope>/proprietary_terms.txt in place, so excluding the tree from
# version control does not weaken the check. The intended arrangement is a
# separate private repository per scope, mounted at projects/<scope>/.
projects/*
!projects/_template/
!projects/README.md

# --- Third-party material not ours to redistribute --------------------------
#
# Published papers and vendor datasheets are cited in references/README.md and
# are to be obtained from their sources. A supplier datasheet in particular is
# not redistributable.
references/*
!references/README.md

# The open Luxtelligence PDK, vendored for convenience during development. It
# is MIT licensed and could be redistributed with its notice, but a documented
# install step is preferred to a 6 MB copy that will drift from upstream.
design-chain/pdk/lxt_pdk_gf/

# Foundry rule decks are obtained from the foundry under their own terms.
design-chain/pdk/LXT_KLayout_DRC_Runsets/

# --- Deliberately tracked ---------------------------------------------------
#
# golden/ holds the layout regression reference. It is binary and it is tracked
# on purpose: `picchain golden` compares against it, and a reference that is not
# under version control is not a reference.
!**/golden/
!**/golden/**

# --- Not published --------------------------------------------------------
#
# Rendered documents. They are generated from the Markdown beside them and go
# stale the moment it is edited, which it frequently is. A stale PDF next to a
# current source is worse than no PDF.
*.pdf

# The operating manuals, wherever they sit. These are instructions to an agent
# rather than documentation of the chain, and they carry working directives that
# are of no use to a reader of the repository. The skills, the sub-agents and the
# lessons ledger under .claude/ ARE published: they hold transferable design
# knowledge and are sanitised.
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md
